== git push forms against the local bare repository
$ git push -u origin feat
To ../remote.git
 * [new branch]      feat -> feat
branch 'feat' set up to track 'origin/feat'.
-> exit 0
$ git push -uf origin feat
Everything up-to-date
branch 'feat' set up to track 'origin/feat'.
-> exit 0
$ git push --delet origin tmp1
To ../remote.git
 - [deleted]         tmp1
-> exit 0
$ git push -d origin tmp2
To ../remote.git
 - [deleted]         tmp2
-> exit 0
$ git push --prune origin refs/heads/*
To ../remote.git
 - [deleted]         tmp3
 * [new branch]      tmp1 -> tmp1
 * [new branch]      tmp2 -> tmp2
-> exit 0
$ git ls-remote --heads origin
